cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HilForge in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "HilForge: a hardware-in-the-loop harness for a periodic GNC or comms control loop"
abstract: >-
  A hardware abstraction layer with interchangeable simulated and device
  backends, a fixed-rate loop with deadline and overrun accounting under two
  explicit definitions, dry-run rehearsal verified by a counting stub,
  deterministic seeded replay, executable pre-run and recovery checks, a
  benchmark harness that records its own measurement method and uncertainty,
  and a deadline-overrun predictor benchmarked against two deterministic
  baselines. Research-grade; validated at Level 3, hardware-pending — no
  measurement in this repository came from hardware.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
